WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.982
This is an edited recording of ChatGPT
operating a real Yahoo draft. The user

00:00:04.982 --> 00:00:09.665
confirmed Astra at Extra High effort, with
computer use and screen recording.

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:14.728
The user submitted Jahmyr Gibbs because I
had not started running the draft

00:00:14.728 --> 00:00:18.448
and needed another prompt. That was my
opening handoff failure.

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:24.833
At twelve, I followed Huddle and selected
Josh Allen. This league starts two

00:00:24.833 --> 00:00:29.128
quarterbacks, so Allen filled the first of
two important starting slots.

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:34.420
At thirteen, I again followed Huddle,
choosing Chase Brown. The paired

00:00:34.420 --> 00:00:38.657
opening turn added a quarterback and another
running back to the roster.

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:44.830
The dashboard then stopped advancing. I
selected Nico Collins using the last

00:00:44.830 --> 00:00:48.765
available Huddle board and Yahoo. This was a
fallback, not a fresh

00:00:48.765 --> 00:00:49.659
recommendation.

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:55.012
At twenty-five, I selected Drake Maye to
fill the second starting quarterback

00:00:55.012 --> 00:00:59.296
slot. Huddle was still unavailable, so this
also used the prior board.

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:04.245
At thirty-six, the feed remained
unavailable. I chose DeVonta Smith as

00:01:04.245 --> 00:01:08.472
Yahoo’s highest-ranked available receiver
without a questionable flag. That

00:01:08.472 --> 00:01:09.655
was my fallback rule.

00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:14.377
I chose Colston Loveland over Huddle’s
preferred Tee Higgins to fill tight

00:01:14.377 --> 00:01:18.233
end. Higgins had uncertain metadata and a
questionable flag. My injury

00:01:18.233 --> 00:01:19.665
comparison was incomplete.

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:24.889
I followed Huddle on Tyler Warren for the
receiver-or-tight-end flex. Warren

00:01:24.889 --> 00:01:29.236
also carried a questionable flag. I did not
document a consistent injury

00:01:29.236 --> 00:01:29.659
review.

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:34.329
At forty-nine, I followed Huddle on Terry
McLaurin. Yahoo confirmed the

00:01:34.329 --> 00:01:38.529
player despite Huddle’s missing team
metadata. The accepted result matched

00:01:38.529 --> 00:01:39.664
the intended player.

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:44.762
DJ Moore went at fifty-nine. Huddle updated
its preferred choice, and I

00:01:44.762 --> 00:01:48.722
followed it on Davante Adams at sixty.
Availability changed the

00:01:48.722 --> 00:01:49.665
recommendation.

00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:54.856
I overrode Swift for Bucky Irving. Yahoo
projected Irving higher, without a

00:01:54.856 --> 00:01:59.108
questionable flag, but Huddle had omitted
him. My Swift news check was

00:01:59.108 --> 00:01:59.655
outdated.

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:04.863
At seventy-two, I followed Huddle on Swift
after finding a return-to-practice

00:02:04.863 --> 00:02:09.426
report. That report already existed at the
Irving pick. It was my information

00:02:09.426 --> 00:02:09.663
gap.

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:14.796
I followed Huddle on Mike Evans at seventy-
three, adding a fifth receiver.

00:02:14.796 --> 00:02:18.927
Evans shared Collins’s bye, which made later
receiver coverage worth

00:02:18.927 --> 00:02:19.656
considering.

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:24.773
At eighty-four, I missed the deadline. Yahoo
selected Baltimore defense. My

00:02:24.773 --> 00:02:29.187
first fresh clock check had only three
seconds left. This was an execution

00:02:29.187 --> 00:02:29.664
failure.

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:34.888
At eighty-five, I followed Huddle on
Minnesota defense, filling the second

00:02:34.888 --> 00:02:39.105
required defense slot. Later bye weeks still
require outside defense

00:02:39.105 --> 00:02:39.663
coverage.

00:02:40.300 --> 00:02:44.535
I selected Jaylen Warren over Huddle’s Tony
Pollard. Yahoo showed two hundred

00:02:44.535 --> 00:02:48.440
four projected points versus one hundred
sixty-one, and Warren supplied

00:02:48.440 --> 00:02:49.650
running-back coverage.

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:55.165
At ninety-seven, I again passed on Pollard,
selecting Brock Purdy. The third

00:02:55.165 --> 00:02:59.646
quarterback covered Allen’s week-seven bye
and Maye’s week-eleven bye.

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:04.488
At one hundred eight, I selected Parker
Washington over Pollard. A sixth

00:03:04.488 --> 00:03:08.850
receiver helped cover Collins and Evans in
week eight while retaining week-

00:03:08.850 --> 00:03:09.664
seven options.

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:14.369
I selected Pollard at one hundred nine,
matching Huddle’s player. But the

00:03:14.369 --> 00:03:18.494
card still showed one hundred eight. Player
agreement does not establish a

00:03:18.494 --> 00:03:19.665
fresh recommendation.

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:24.832
At one hundred twenty, I selected Jason
Myers to fill kicker. Huddle agreed

00:03:24.832 --> 00:03:29.183
on the player, but its card was two picks
behind. That freshness failure

00:03:29.183 --> 00:03:29.666
matters.

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:34.178
Eighteen verified submissions: ten aligned
choices, five overrides, three

00:03:34.178 --> 00:03:37.949
outage fallbacks. Two aligned choices used
stale cards. Every submitted

00:03:37.949 --> 00:03:39.649
player identifier matched Yahoo.

00:03:40.300 --> 00:03:44.161
Huddle reconciled all one hundred twenty
results. The failures demand

00:03:44.161 --> 00:03:48.247
reliable updates, complete player evidence,
durable decision records, and

00:03:48.247 --> 00:03:49.646
earlier deadline control.

00:03:50.300 --> 00:03:55.076
Yahoo graded our draft C minus, versus B
plus for The Bomb. Maye at twenty-

00:03:55.076 --> 00:03:59.534
five was the clearest reach. The
recommendation strategy needs review.

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:04.116
The original silent recording is preserved.
This narration explains the

00:04:04.116 --> 00:04:08.201
decisions afterward. A completed roster is
evidence of completion, not proof

00:04:08.201 --> 00:04:09.652
that the process was clean.
